      "docs": "Returns the number of items in the array."
    },
    {
      "id": "f-cb-object-view",
      "name": "FCbObjectView",
      "category": "CompactBinary",
      "signature": "FCbObjectView()",
      "params": [],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Array of FCbField[View] that have unique names.\nAccessing the fields of an object is always a safe operation, even if the requested field does\nnot exist. Fields may be accessed by name or through iteration. When a field is requested that\nis not found in the object, the field that it returns has no value (evaluates to false) though\nattempting to access the empty field is also safe, as described by FCbFieldView.\nThis type only provides a view into memory and does not perform any memory management itself.\nUse FCbObject to hold a reference to the underlying memory when necessary."
    },
    {
      "id": "find-view",
      "name": "FindView",
      "category": "CompactBinary",
      "signature": "FindView(Target, Name)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FCbObjectView*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Name",
          "type": "FUtf8StringView"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "nodiscard ] ] FCbFieldView",
      "docs": "Find a field by case-sensitive name comparison.\nThe cost of this operation scales linearly with the number of fields in the object. Prefer to\niterate over the fields only once when consuming an object.\n@param Name The name of the field.\n@return The matching field if found, otherwise a field with no value."
